[l_english.STATE_LORE_56]
Centaurs and gargoyles are two completely different beings. Centaurs represent strength and wisdom, while gargoyles prefer magic and art. Fate has brought them to the same continent, painting a strange picture.
A thousand years ago, the prince of the centaurs and the princess of the gargoyles were married in a grand ceremony, ending the conflict between the two races, and ushering in a millennium of prosperity and peace. A thousand years later, the two benevolent rulers were old, and their proud subjects were already dissatisfied with the status quo: the elders in power performing witchcraft in the dark of night, the noble youths quarreling in taverns, the queen's followers protesting silently, and the outlander refugees whispering in dark alleys. Though, no faction could have predicted that the greatest upheaval in this kingdom would come from the vibrant and energetic crown prince.
The magic-savvy mentor Sendak saw infinite potential in Prince Tirek, secretly planting the seeds of power hunger in his mind. Yet, the prince’s desire to explore magical knowledge far exceeded the mentor’s expectations. Out of greed for magic, the immature apprentice impatiently experimented on slaves from another continent. In an accidental magical explosion, the conspiracy between Sendak and the elders was exposed, and the prince was expelled as a culprit involved. The young Tirek did not miss his homeland, nor did he yearn for the affluent life of being a prince, nor did he care about the people who denounced him. The only thing etched in his mind that he could not get rid of was the resolute and disappointed look in the eyes of his father, King Vorak, when he sentenced him to exile. He could not understand why his own kin would give up on their own son for the sake of a slave from another race and a conspiracy that had nothing to do with Tirek.
“Only by pursuing greater power can I prove my worth to the old guy.” The seed in his mind grew into a towering tree, and Tirek embarked on a journey to seek power. On this long road of corruption, he fell out with his younger brother Scorpan, was betrayed when success was within reach, spent hundreds of years in prison, experienced another failure, and finally obtained the power he had been dreaming of.
“Look! Father, at this point, would you still feel disappointed instead of proud?” Tirek returned to his homeland as a king, seized the throne from his weak and indifferent father Vorak, punished his brother Scorpan who betrayed him, and hunted down his mentor Sendak who fled in fear of punishment.

Yet at the very end, he never saw a trace of emotion in his father's eyes other than scorn.

[l_simp_chinese.STATE_LORE_56]
半人马与石像鬼是两个截然不同的存在，半人马代表着力量与智慧，而石像鬼则偏好魔法与艺术。但命运却让他们诞生在同一片大陆上，绘制出了一幅奇异的画卷。
千年前，半人马的王子与石像鬼的公主在盛大的仪式中结为夫妻，终结了两族的纷争，为两个种族开启了持续千年的繁荣与和平。千年后，两位仁慈的统治者年事已高，骄傲的臣民们却早已不满于现状：手握大权的长老们在黑夜中修行作法，贵族的子弟们在酒馆中争吵，王后的追随者们在无声地抗议，外族的流民则在阴暗的巷尾窃窃私语。但没有一方势力可以预料到，这个王国最重大的变故，是那朝气蓬勃富有活力的大王子。
精通魔法的导师僧达克从提雷克王子的身上看到了无穷的潜力，在他的思想中偷偷种下了渴求力量的种子。但这位王子对魔法知识的探索欲望也远远超出了导师的预期，对魔法的贪婪让幼稚的学徒急不可耐地对来自另一片大陆的奴隶做起了实验。在意外的魔法爆炸中，僧达克与长老们月下的阴谋暴露，王子也成为了牵连其中的罪人被逐出了王国。年轻的提雷克并不思念家乡，并不怀念身为王子的富庶生活，也并不在乎那些声讨他的民众。唯一烙印在他脑海中挥之不去的，是他的父亲沃拉克国王宣判驱逐他时的决绝与眼神中的失望。他无法理解为何自己的至亲宁愿为了另一种族的奴隶和与提雷克完全无关的阴谋而放弃自己的亲儿子。
“唯有追求更强大的力量，才能向那个老家伙证明我的价值。” 思想中的种子成长为了参天大树，提雷克踏上了追寻力量的旅途。在这漫长的堕落之路中，他与亲弟弟斯科潘反目成仇，在成功唾手可得之际遭遇背叛，在牢狱中度过了数百年光阴，经历了再一次的失败，并最终如愿以偿获得了他梦寐以求的力量。
“看呐！父亲，事到如今你还会感到失望而不是骄傲吗？” 提雷克以王者的姿态回归故土，夺取了那软弱而冷漠的父亲沃拉克的王位，惩罚了那背叛他的弟弟斯科潘，通缉了那畏罪潜逃的导师僧达克。

但他终究没有看到父亲眼神中除蔑视之外一丝一毫的情绪。
